dialect protocol
protocol svg.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.svg
start body

# P2-FG3: `stdio.svg` is TEXT-NATIVE (per the W0 census row) -- there is no "binary SVG"; the pack
# container IS the SEMIO envelope wrapping the artifact's own real wire text verbatim
# (`ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with` in ../../🦀️.rs: `write_svg_xml(&self.doc).into_bytes()`
# passed straight to `store::semio_format::wrap_binary` -- no `pack_rt::encode_document` structured
# record, because the persisted `doc: XmlDocument` field is a genuinely recursive, data-carrying
# enum tree with no `RecordSpec` to walk against, same reason `#[derive(dsl::DslArtifact)]` is
# unusable here, identical root cause to `📰️xml`'s own sibling protocol file). Replaces the
# pre-Phase-2 placeholder that (falsely) described the payload as a JSON serialization of the doc --
# the real codec was fixed this wave to stop routing through `serde_json` at all (see
# `../../🦀️.rs`'s `ArtifactPack` impl doc comment), so this file's own description now
# matches reality.
#
# The framework-level SEMIO envelope itself (magic `0x8953454D0D0A1A0A` + LE u32 token length +
# UTF-8 token) is described ONCE, at
# `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio`
# (P2-M3 deliverable 3) -- this file does NOT re-describe that framing. Cross-artifact
# `use semio.envelope` is not yet functional (confirmed unchanged through every pilot, see
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.1), so the envelope is deliberately NOT re-inlined here either -- this
# file models the bytes as if the walk already starts AT the payload, past the envelope, matching
# how `m5_handcrafted_protocol_conformance`'s own harness unwraps the envelope before handing bytes
# to `walk_protocol`.
#
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY layer by construction (its
# real internal grammar -- element/attribute/content-node recursion, restated from xml's own shape
# -- is ../📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio's job, not the protocol dialect's) -- `chain ... utf8`
# is the honest boundary, the same treatment json's/xml's own snapshot protocol give their text
# payload.
framing record
chain payload utf8
